Make diff exit with status 2 when a directory entry can't be examined.
When diff lists a directory, recursive_action() warns about an entry it
can't stat, such as a broken symbolic link, or a subdirectory it can't
open, and leaves it out of the listing. diff ignored the failure, so
apart from the warning the entry was as good as absent, and the exit
status could be 0. Record error status 2 when recursive_action()
reports a failure, as diffutils does for a file it can't examine.

---
 editors/diff.c |    6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/editors/diff.c
+++ b/editors/diff.c
@@ -915,9 +915,11 @@
 		 * Using list.len to specify its length,
 		 * add_to_dirlist will remove it. */
 		list[i].len = strlen(p[i]);
-		recursive_action(p[i], ACTION_RECURSE |
+		/* An entry that can't be examined was reported and left out */
+		if (!recursive_action(p[i], ACTION_RECURSE |
 			((option_mask32 & FLAG(no_deref)) ? 0 : ACTION_FOLLOWLINKS),
-				add_to_dirlist, skip_dir, &list[i]);
+				add_to_dirlist, skip_dir, &list[i]))
+			exit_status |= 2;
 		/* Sort dl alphabetically.
 		 * GNU diff does this ignoring any number of trailing dots.
 		 * We don't, so for us dotted files almost always are
